    </codeType>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBuildings adjoining areas of open space (particularly in residential developments) \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Ebe oriented to maximise views to and across these spaces. In addition to promoting good passive surveillance, this orientation enhances visual and physical connections to nature. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EException:\u003C/strong\u003E Where orienting a building towards the open space would prevent it from providing frontage onto the street, the layout \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Ebalance both objectives to maintain street enclosure and surveillance whilst maximising views to the open space.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
